    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There are only two test files plus the base (`AcceptanceTest`, `AcceptanceBase`), and the build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness rejection for owner creation, following the codebase's existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signaling the business-rule conflict, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `assertEmailUnique(owner, owner.getEmail())` into `saveOwner` (right after the telephone check) and a new private `assertEmailUnique` method that scans all owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` when another owner shares the same normalized (lower-cased) email. Email is already normalized to lowercase earlier in `saveOwner` via `normalizeEmail`, so the comparison is case-insensitive as specified.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 registered an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that returns **409 Conflict**, consistent with the other duplicate/conflict handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create owner A with an email, then create owner B with the same email \u2192 expects 409) passes, and the full test suite is green.",
