        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive clone of the codebase's existing duplicate-field pattern.\n\n- `DuplicateEmailException` mirrors the sibling `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateHouseholdException` exceptions in the same `service` package \u2014 same `RuntimeException` base, same message style, same Javadoc noting the 409 mapping.\n- `assertEmailUnique` is a structural twin of the adjacent `assertTelephoneUnique` (same null/empty guard, same self-exclusion by id, same `normalizeEmail(...)` reuse), placed directly after it, and reuses the existing `normalizeEmail` helper rather than duplicating normalization logic.\n- The call site in `saveOwner` sits right after `assertTelephoneUnique`, matching the established ordering of validation asserts.\n- The `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler follows the same `@ExceptionHandler` + `detailBuild` + `logger.warn` shape as the neighboring duplicate handlers.\n\nLogic is in the right unit (uniqueness rule in the service, HTTP mapping in the advice), nothing is duplicated, and no class is turning into a catch-all. A maintainer would find this entirely natural."
